  "narrative": {
    "essence": "Canada qualified for consecutive World Cups for the first time in history and is hosting this one alongside the USA and Mexico. After a disappointing exit in 2022, this squad — filled with stars from Europe's biggest leagues — returns hungry, on home soil, with something to prove.",
    "footballIdentity": "Canada's football story is only just being written. For decades this was hockey country, full stop. But a generation of Canadians grew up playing in academies across Europe, and the talent pipeline finally produced a squad competitive enough to reach back-to-back World Cups. Alphonso Davies is the symbol: a refugee who became the best left-back in the world. Canada football is about becoming.",
    "theMoment": "Canada co-hosts the 2026 World Cup, with games in Toronto and Vancouver. This is the sport arriving in Canada's own backyard — a country that has never had a men's team worth watching and now has one worth following. The pressure on Jesse Marsch after the 2022 group stage exit is real. The talent is undeniable. The question is whether the system and the moment align.",
    "momentType": "footballing"
