    "tacticalNote": "Marsch's Canada presses aggressively and relies on the pace of Davies and Buchanan to create chaos. David operates as a center-forward who finishes the attacks the wide players generate. The press is designed to win the ball high and attack immediately — Canada is at their best in transition.",
    "strength": "Width and pace — Davies and Buchanan can exploit any team with high defensive lines, and David is lethal when through on goal.",
